<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War · Crisis</p><h1 class="enc-title">War of the Jülich Succession</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1609–1614</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Jülich succession crisis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The War of the Jülich Succession was a dispute over the United Duchies of Jülich-Cleves-Berg after the death of the childless Duke John William in 1609. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palatinate-neuburg">Palatinate-Neuburg</a>, backed by Protestant and Catholic allies, contested the inheritance, which nearly set off a general European war. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-xanten">Treaty of Xanten</a> of 1614 divided the lands, giving <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kleve">Cleves</a>, Mark and Ravensberg to Brandenburg.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/war-of-the-julich-succession.jpg" alt="War of the Jülich Succession" width="320" height="263" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gankbank789 · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:War_of_the_J%C3%BClich_Succession.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
